[00:21.47] The workadays were propping the bar quietly erasing the week and
[00:29.71] I was in the corner booth thinking (pretending to read)
[00:37.48] About the possibility of one to love unconditionally and the words that
[00:48.95] Drive into the ground their repetition starts to thin their meaning.
[01:08.01] Then everything got frighteningly still as they entered and intersected the
[01:15.13] Floor and I tried to choke my stare at the perfection that others would kill for.
[01:24.71] But all of the parts are the same on every face (few variables change)
[01:34.77] The differences pale when compared to the similarities they share.
[01:47.39] Finally there is clarity and there is purpose after all, but every night
[02:00.39] Ends the same as I'm collapsing once more by your side.
[02:09.09] Finally there is clarity: This tiny life is making sense,
[02:18.92] And every drop numbs the both of us, but I alone am staggering.
[04:30.34] 